1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,686
Question fourteen.

2
00:00:01,686 --> 00:00:08,242
Step one: macro scan. It asks storage for Hello in standard A S C I I.

3
00:00:08,242 --> 00:00:12,175
One mark. Command words: “storage needed”.

4
00:00:12,175 --> 00:00:13,861
Step two: denoise.

5
00:00:13,861 --> 00:00:17,139
Useful, in yellow: Hello, one byte.

6
00:00:17,139 --> 00:00:21,821
In cyan: “standard A S C I I” and “per character”.

7
00:00:21,821 --> 00:00:26,972
Useless red herring: what the word means — kick it out.

8
00:00:26,972 --> 00:00:28,658
Step three: draft.

9
00:00:28,658 --> 00:00:31,655
H, e, l, l, o — five characters.

10
00:00:31,655 --> 00:00:33,528
Five times one byte.

11
00:00:33,528 --> 00:00:34,558
Five bytes.

12
00:00:34,558 --> 00:00:36,150
Step four: P O E.

13
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:40,365
B, six bytes: extra terminator counted — cut.

14
00:00:40,365 --> 00:00:44,673
C, ten bytes: treated as two bytes each — cut.

15
00:00:44,673 --> 00:00:48,232
D, forty bytes: counted in bits — cut.

16
00:00:48,232 --> 00:00:55,911
Step five: sanity check and lock. Five characters, one byte each — the count fits.

17
00:00:55,911 --> 00:00:58,440
So the correct answer is A.

